OL,3,GNEWSAEastenders star launches books
OL,4,Aabout mascots to get kids reading
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn an effort to boost reading and
OL,7,Fliteracy in Stoke-on-Trent, children's
OL,8,Fauthor and former Eastenders actor Tom
OL,9,FWatt has written a series of books
OL,10,Ffeaturing mascots from the city's
OL,11,Ffootball teams.
OL,13,FNew government figures show the number
OL,14,Fof children reading for pleasure is at
OL,15,Fa 20-year-low nationally.
OL,17,FIn Stoke-on-Trent, only 70% of children
OL,18,Fmeet the expected reading level by the
OL,19,Fend of primary school, while the
OL,20,Fnational average is 75%.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
